# Rebuild for QA

After a change QA can exercise (install, launch, saves, catalog, GUI, server, or client behavior), rebuild before finishing. Docs-only and comment-only edits do not need a rebuild.

From the repo root:

```
powershell -File scripts/build-windows.ps1
powershell -File scripts/build-windows-xp.ps1
wsl -e bash scripts/build-linux.sh
```

Outputs:

- `build-windows\bin` — current Windows client (`vapor-gui.exe`, `vapor.exe`, `vapor-selftest.exe`)
- `build-windows-xp\bin` — Windows XP SP3 client; copy that whole directory
- `build-linux/bin` — `vapord`, `vapor-admin`, and the Linux client

If WSL or the MinGW XP toolchain is missing, say which build did not run. Report the directories and binary names when the builds finish.
